  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "DEATH 1906 REFUTED (research 2026-07-03): Vincenza did NOT die in 1906. Her daughter Mary's original Apr 1939 SS-5 (SSN 017-12-5027, NARA NUMIDENT) names 'father ANGELO PROSPER; mother VA MINNICHEILLO', and son John Louis Prosper's SS-5 (b. 21 Jun 1908 Brockton) names 'mother VIRGINIA MINICHELLO' — she was alive and bearing children in Brockton from 1902 through at least 16 Aug 1917. The sourced 1910-1927 Brockton residences are genuinely hers. The 1906 Boston 'Vincenza Prospero' death is a mis-attachment — possibly an infant daughter named for her, or an unrelated family; needs the MA 1906 death register.",
      "NAME: Americanized as 'Virginia' (why the census wife looked like a different woman from 'Vincenza'). Surname properly MINICHIELLO (SS-5 spellings Minnicheillo/Minichello/Minnichello; the export's 'Minochelli' is another variant). Minichiello is a Campanian surname, heaviest in Avellino province, ~5% Molise — compatible with the DNA journey's North Isernia origin but not proof; Angelo's naturalization/manifest is the decisive record.",
      "CHILDREN CORRECTED: hers are those from the 8 Jan 1902 marriage onward — Rosa (~1902), Carl (~1905), Toby (~1906), John Louis (b. 21 Jun 1908), Dominic (~1910), Delia L (~1911), Philomena (~1913), Louise Theresa (b. 18 Nov 1915, per SS-5 — not ~1916), Mary Elizabeth (b. 16 Aug 1917). Michael (~1889), Anthony (~1891) and Julia (~1894) are children of Angelo's FIRST wife Delia Lawrence (m. Boston 21 May 1889).",
      "OPEN: her actual death date/burial (no NUMIDENT death entry — consistent with dying before the SSDI era or never holding an SSN; likely Calvary Cemetery, Brockton). Also open: birth comune in Italy.",
      "Sources: NARA AAD NUMIDENT RG 47 (SS-5 files, quoted from full record displays) — aad.archives.gov/aad/series-description.jsp?s=5057."
    ]
  }
